WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.082
Machine learning code commonly separates the input features from the target.

00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:09.262
X is the feature matrix.

00:00:09.262 --> 00:00:11.322
y is the target vector.

00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:18.082
In our example, X contains visits, pages viewed, past orders, and days since the last activity.

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.035
The target is responded.

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:22.907
Run the code and inspect the shapes.

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:27.487
Each row in X corresponds to one target value in y.

00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:31.412
Also look at the first feature vector as a NumPy array.

00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:34.452
This makes the matrix idea concrete.

00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:39.827
It is extremely important that the target does not accidentally appear inside X.

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:46.492
If the answer is included as an input, the model will appear to perform very well for the wrong reason.

00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:49.233
That is a simple example of data leakage.
